# intelligent monitoring system collects measurements from two sensors. The covariance 
matrix of the measurements is 
C =[ 5 2
2 2 ] 
The system uses eigenvalue and eigenvector analysis to identify the principal direction of 
variation in the sensor data. 
Write a Python program using NumPy to calculate the eigenvalues and eigenvectors, identify 
the eigenvector corresponding to the largest eigenvalue, and use Matplotlib to visualize both 
eigenvectors as arrows on a two-dimensional graph.






import numpy as np

C = np.array([[5,2],[2,2]])
v, V = np.linalg.eig(C)
i = np.argmax(v)
print("Largest eigenvalue:", v[i])
print("Principal vector:", V[:,i])
